  "description": "Finds form script problems that nothing else reports: a handler calling a function the\n      declared library does not define, a library that is missing or empty, a handler using a\n      library the form never loads, and controls bound to columns that no longer exist.\n\n      These failures are silent. The solution imports cleanly, nothing is logged, and the first\n      sign of trouble is an error dialog in a user's face.\n\n      The scan runs against your own publisher prefixes, so Microsoft's own forms - whose scripts\n      are bundled inside the platform and cannot be resolved from a web resource - are left alone.\n      Findings export to CSV.",
